  <div class="card-desc">Error Level Analysis detects regions with inconsistent JPEG compression — a technique used in forensic contexts to identify locally edited or composited areas. <strong style="color:#f59e0b;">Note:</strong> images that have been processed in Lightroom and exported as JPEG (as most in this library are) will naturally score higher than unedited camera originals. This is expected — Lightroom applies sharpening, noise reduction, and local adjustments that create compression-level variation across regions. A high score here reflects <em>editing activity</em>, not AI generation or deceptive manipulation. Use it as a relative signal — outliers with an unusually high score compared to the rest of your library are worth a closer look. The extreme outlier count above uses a 3×IQR fence: any image whose max error exceeds Q3 + 3 × (Q3 − Q1), where Q1 and Q3 are your library's 25th and 75th percentile scores, is flagged. This adapts to your library's own baseline rather than a fixed cutoff.</div>
